ld have sent the second tiger berserk  killing that soldier the scene was an  alternative way of introducing the idea  that the explorers were setting in  motion events that would disrupt the  local ecosystem they had no idea about  other weird and wonderful creatures cut  from the movie include a monster Venus  flytrap by the way interestingly a Venus  flytrap monster already appeared in the  animated Kong TV series wreck battled  and nearly defeated Kong in the episode  green fear and the art and making of  Kong Skull Island  has some very cool a news concept art of  other creatures and monsters we never  got to see in the final film a number of  unused designs exist the creature  below the water and others that live on  the land although dinosaurs have  featured in previous Kong films such as  the 1933 and 2005 movies vogt-roberts  was adamant that dinosaurs shouldn't  appear in Kong Skull Island the director  said he didn't want to try and rival the  Jurassic Park and world movies and he  wanted his creatures not to feel too  alien like in the end the closer he got  to a dinosaur in the final movie with a  Triceratops skull director vogt-roberts  also wanted the indigenous population  and where they live to feel fresh and  different from previous Kong movies but  before the Erie Village we see in the  final movie two alternative indigenous  settlements were planned the first is  going to be the boat city where people  lived among boats and other ships that  have washed up on the island the second  village was going to be known as Kong  City and it was planned as a traditional  tribal village that was built into rocks  and caverns it was a place where the  people literally worshipped Kong you  would sit like a king on the throne in  front of them the concept art for Kong  city looks epic and although it doesn't  make it into the final movie there is a  nod to the original idea in the stone  paintings of the eerie worshipping Kong  that we see after Conrad and the team  meet Marlow a different ending to the  movie was also considered which would  have featured a bigger role for the  eerie people the alternate ending  involved a desperate action scene with a  team stuck on Marlo's boat while being  attacked by a skull crawler in the scene  the skull crawlers have broken through  the wall and the boat ends up trapped at  the dead end of the river  the only way to escape is for the eerie  villagers to haul the boat up over a  rock face and waterfall and into another  river to get them to safety the scene  was inspired by directors Verna  Hertzog's 1982 film Fitzcarraldo about  her rubber baron who plans to use native  people to drag a huge steam ship over  the side of a mountain in the Amazon  basin as well as an alternate ending  there were also alternate post-credit  scenes in one of them Conrad and Weaver  end up on a boat in the Arctic Ocean  together with Brooke as they watch the  ocean Godzilla suddenly rises up through  the layer of ice  although this would have been pretty  cool the idea was rejected as they  realized the scene would have been  inconsistent with the timeline set in  the 2014 Godzilla movie the main story  in Kong Skull Island takes place in the  1970s and in the Godzilla film it was  reported that Godzilla hadn't appeared  since the atomic bomb  test of the 19:15 now I'd love to know  what you thought about the deleted  scenes and creatures we never got to see  in Kong Skull Island and are there any  kaiju you'd love to see appear in a  future Kong or Godzilla movie let me  know in the comments below if you  enjoyed this and do hit that like button  and why not check out some more of my  movie deleted scenes right here thanks  for watching and see you next time  yippee-ki-yay movie lovers
 

